  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tCapium 365\n\t\tCapium 365 (Accountant)\n\n### Capium 365: Invoices How to publish in Bookkeeping\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Mon, 21 Jul, 2025 at  3:29 PM\n\n\t\tIn order to publish your Invoices from Capium 365 into your Bookkeeping module, follow the navigation below:\n\nNavigation: Capium 365 > [Specific Client] >Inovices\n\nFor invoices, Credit Notes you can follow the below steps:\n\n1. Firstly, you have to approve any invoices with the thumb icon:\n\n2. After clicking this icon, a pop-up will appear: \n\na) In this pop-up you can either press 'Yes', or you can press 'Approve & Publish', which will immediately publish it into your Bookkeeping module. \n\nPlease refer the below Screenshot:\n\n If you only clicked 'Yes', you still have an opportunity to publish to Bookkeeping by selecting the icon:\n\nTo unpublish, simply click the same publish icon again. \n\nYou will also see the following actions available:\n\nEdit – Modify invoice/credit note details.\n\nApprove / Withdraw Approval – Approve or revoke approval status.\n\nPublish / Unpublish – Push or remove from Bookkeeping.\n\nExport – Download the invoice/credit note.\n\nNote: if you are unable to approve a transaction, double check that in the details of the invoice, an account name has been designated to the product or service.\n\nWant an overview of Invoices and other Areas with that? \n\nFor a more detailed guide on how to add or bulk upload invoices, please see the help article below: \n\nLINK\n\nhttps://capium.freshdesk.com/a/solutions/articles/9000268872?portalId=9000044273\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
